body:
The incremental sync tests cover UTF-16 edge cases (emoji, accented characters) but don't test CRLF line endings. While the implementation appears correct for CRLF (it strips `\r` before UTF-16 conversion and includes it in byte offset calculation), adding a test would provide confidence and prevent regressions.

Consider adding a test like:
```rust
#[test]
fn test_incremental_crlf_line_endings() {
    let mut state = ServerState::new();
    let uri = DocumentUri::new("file:///test/doc.md").unwrap();
    // Use CRLF line endings
    state.open_document(uri.clone(), "# Title\r\n\r\nContent".to_string());

    state.apply_document_changes(
        &uri,
        vec![DocumentChange::Incremental {
            start_line: 2,
            start_character: 7,  // End of "Content"
            end_line: 2,
            end_character: 7,
            text: " more".to_string(),
        }],
    );

    assert_eq!(state.get_document_text(&uri), Some("# Title\r\n\r\nContent more"));
}
```
